<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George Seferis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1900–1971</span> · Also known as Giorgos Seferis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George Seferis, born Giorgos Seferiadis near Smyrna, was a Greek poet and diplomat. His collections, beginning with Strophe in 1931, combined modernist technique with Greek history and myth and the experience of the lost Greek world of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia-minor">Asia Minor</a>. In 1963 he became the first Greek to win the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-prize">Nobel Prize</a> in Literature, and in 1969 he publicly condemned the military junta.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-seferis.jpg" alt="George Seferis" width="320" height="505" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:George_Seferis.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
